{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And the sons of Judah: Er and Onan, etc.</b> One needs to know for what purpose Scripture mentions them, since they had already died? Also, there is nothing novel in informing us of their death. Also, one must examine the verse's saying <b>and the sons of Perez were</b>, etc. — it should have said ״and the sons of Perez״ etc., as it says afterward ״and the sons of Beriah״; what is its intent in saying <b>were</b> etc.? And it is possible that according to what we established earlier concerning the mitzvah of yibbum — that it brings the soul of the deceased — and given the reality before us that Er and Onan died without children, and the levir is required to bring them, behold Judah acted as levir on behalf of Shelah and brought the two souls themselves, and Scripture informs us that Er and Onan stand in their place, for Hezron and Hamul entered in their stead, and this is the gist of the verse: ״And the sons of Judah, five sons: Er and Onan etc. and he died״ etc., and accordingly Er and Onan returned to being sons of Perez — Hezron and Hamul — for they returned to the world gestated in the sod of the soul of the deceased, and they became Hezron and Hamul." "<b>And by way of</b> peshat, Scripture may intend by mentioning Er and Onan to advocate merit on their behalf, for the reason Er and Onan died was because they were in the land of Canaan, in the manner of the verse's saying (Leviticus 18:3) ״כְּמַעֲשֵׂה אֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם וּכְמַעֲשֵׂה אֶרֶץ כְּנָעַן״ etc., and they said, their memory for blessing (Leviticus Rabbah, chapter 23): Scripture equated the deeds of Egypt etc. And because Er and Onan were there, they learned from their deeds; but apart from this, the sons of that righteous man have no evil and bitter root, God forbid. And you will find that the Elohim of Israel commanded not to learn from them, as it is written ״כְּמַעֲשֵׂה״ etc." "<b>And the reason</b> for saying <b>were</b> — it alludes that to these the term הֲוָיָה (ongoing existence) applies, and there are none like them in death, because from them will come forth a shoot to Jesse, our Mashiach our King, who will be for a banner of the nations; to him the nations will seek."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :register {:flags {1 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:49:12.841361491Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}